Short:        AGA graphics and Bob engine for AMOS Pro
Author:       HWARF (Jerome)
Uploader:     amethist rumor786 passinbox com (Jerome)
Type:         dev/amos
Version:      0.14.0 (M19 P2d, 21 Nov 2026)
Requires:     AMOS Professional, AGA chipset, 68020+
Architecture: m68k-amigaos
Distribution: Aminet

Description:
  AMOSPro AGA Extension is an unofficial graphics extension for
  AMOS Professional on AGA-equipped Commodore Amiga computers
  (including A1200/A4000) and AGA-enabled WinUAE. It extends
  the original AMOS editor and interpreter, without replacing them.

  Version 0.14.0 / M19 P2d provides 100 native AMOS commands and
  functions (203 AP20 entries). Motorola 68020 or better required.

  Features carried forward from 0.13.27:
    - Indexed AGA screens (2 to 256 colours), double buffering
    - IFF/ILBM loading, AGAPIC banks, palettes, fades and cycling
    - Safe Blitter graphics, Copper raster effects and 2D drawing
    - Text, AMCAF font-bank selection, mouse and keyboard input
    - Fast Icons, Chip RAM CBlock capture and restoration
    - Chunky-to-planar C2P, including Blit and Zoom
    - Direct IFF-to-chunky decoding into an AMOS DATA/WORK bank

  New M19 software Bob engine, P0 to P2:
    - Multi-image AGBO banks, transparency/masks, positioning,
      hot spots, priority, per-page restoration and cleanup
    - Bob image selection and safe bank cache release
    - Aga Bob Col: rectangle or opaque-pixel mask collision
    - Aga Bob Flip: normal, H, V and H+V orientations
    - Aga Bob Planes: destination bitplane selection
    - Aga Bob Auto Update: automatic draw before guarded Swap
    - AMAL memory bridge: two synchronous AMAL channels driving
      separate AGA Bobs without a new AMAL extension command

  New demonstration: BOB_ALL_IN_ONE.asc
    - Self-contained asymmetric F/L graphics in 16x16 and 32x32
    - Animated Bobs, collisions, flips, bitplanes and auto update
    - No external graphics files required; uses AMOS banks 24/27/28
    - Separate RAM logs for Runtime, Compiler and interpreted mode

  Validation (WinUAE, exact M19 P2d library and example):
    - Runtime Gate B: PASS, RESULT 1, ERR 0
    - Real AMOS Compiler Gate C: PASS, RESULT 1, ERR 0
    - 240 valid AMAL cycles, 252 successful Swaps per run
    - 8 collision checks, 20 Flip and 10 Planes pixel checks
    - Screen cleanup/Close successful in both modes
    - 121 initial Swap refusals per run, all recovered after
      one additional VBL; not a zero-refusal or speed guarantee
    - Physical AGA hardware and strict interpreted mode untested
    - Not all historical extension APIs retested in these runs

  IMPORTANT - external C2P dependency:
    The five Aga C2P commands require c2p.library v1.9,
    installed separately in LIBS: (usually SYS:Libs/).
    It is NOT part of AMOSPro_AGA.Lib. Obtain it from Aminet:
      https://aminet.net/package/dev/misc/c2plib
    Aga Iff To Chunky and the Bob features do not require it.

  Installation:
    1. Back up your AMOS configuration and installed libraries.
    2. Copy AMOSPro_AGA.Lib into your AMOS APSystem directory.
    3. In AMOS Pro: Config / Set Interpreter /
       Set Loaded Extensions, select an available slot.
       Keep the existing slot when upgrading (historically 14).
    4. Save the interpreter configuration and restart AMOS.
    5. Install c2p.library v1.9 in LIBS: only for C2P commands.
    6. Import .asc files with Project / Merge ASCII.

  Exact release library:
    M19 P2d, 136020 bytes, SHA256:
    ce5fb614c7acae9b1bb88e1d793d73dbe7ba747edc285acb7d9e72ac3104176f
    Internal binary ID remains "$VER: AMOSPro_AGA M19 P2d".

  Documentation, sources and latest examples:
    https://github.com/anthea176/AMOSPro-AGA-Extension

  This release completes the software Bob milestone. Hardware AGA
  Sprites are planned next, but are NOT included in this version.

